To,
The Station House Officer,
Cyber Crime Police Station, Bengaluru City

Subject: Complaint regarding online fraud of Rs. 1,45,000

Sir,
I, Priya Nair, aged 34, W/o Anil Nair, resident of 12, 4th Cross, Indiranagar, Bengaluru, submit that on 03 March 2026 I received a call from mobile number 9900112233 from a person who introduced himself as an executive of HDFC Bank and said my KYC would expire. He sent a link and asked for my Aadhaar 2345 6789 0124 and PAN BXQPN4821K. Thereafter Rs 1,45,000 was debited from my account number 50100234567891 (IFSC HDFC0001234) on 03/03/2026 at 16:42 hrs. The amount was transferred to UPI ID ramesh.kumar88@okaxis and later to account 917020045612345 of Axis Bank. The caller also emailed me from support.hdfc.verify@gmail.com. The suspect used the name Ramesh Kumar. Transaction ID 604512398712.
I request registration of FIR under Section 66C, 66D of the IT Act and Section 318(4) BNS.
Yours faithfully,
Priya Nair
Mobile: 098450 11223
